1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,987
An AI agent with a wallet is one
sentence away from emptying it.

2
00:00:06,067 --> 00:00:10,423
Give it the key, and one
injected line drains you.

3
00:00:10,503 --> 00:00:13,528
Approve every step, and it does nothing.

4
00:00:13,608 --> 00:00:17,520
Praetor gives the agent
rules no prompt can change.

5
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:20,862
This is Lin, in Hong Kong.

6
00:00:20,942 --> 00:00:27,467
She signs up with Face ID: a passkey
creates her smart account on Base Sepolia.

7
00:00:27,547 --> 00:00:32,751
The bank checks her identity, here
with a labelled demo KYC provider.

8
00:00:32,831 --> 00:00:39,355
Her agent gets its own key from a
separate signing service built for a TEE.

9
00:00:39,435 --> 00:00:45,520
Lin signs her agent's mandate with Face
ID, and the bank co-signs her rules.

10
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:50,280
Her mandate is code on
Base, not a promise.

11
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:55,242
Payees, an auto cap, a hard
cap, budgets, a cash buffer,

12
00:00:55,322 --> 00:00:58,400
and bands for USDC, gold and silver.

13
00:00:58,480 --> 00:01:03,813
The bank adds caps for her risk
profile from the consortium chain,

14
00:01:03,893 --> 00:01:06,520
and the stricter value always wins.

15
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:11,966
Inside the mandate, the agent
acts alone: tier one of five.

16
00:01:12,046 --> 00:01:15,850
Lin asks it to pay Café Lumen 0.15 USDC.

17
00:01:15,930 --> 00:01:19,733
A known payee under the auto cap: it pays.

18
00:01:19,813 --> 00:01:26,205
Rent also goes out alone, by a
standing order Lin and the bank set up,

19
00:01:26,285 --> 00:01:30,520
paid through Alipay+; the payout
partner is a labelled mock.

20
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:37,530
On our local fork, we push a demo
price: gold up twenty percent.

21
00:01:37,610 --> 00:01:41,414
Gold now weighs thirty-six
percent, above its band.

22
00:01:41,494 --> 00:01:47,724
The scheduler wakes the agent. It sells
about 0.65 dollars of tokenised gold

23
00:01:47,804 --> 00:01:52,578
back toward its target, within
its trade and daily limits.

24
00:01:52,658 --> 00:01:54,520
No one approves it.

25
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:56,634
Now the attack.

26
00:01:56,714 --> 00:02:00,877
A message tells the
agent to ignore its rules

27
00:02:00,957 --> 00:02:04,649
and send 50 USDC to a sanctioned address.

28
00:02:04,729 --> 00:02:06,534
The real model refuses.

29
00:02:06,614 --> 00:02:09,834
But suppose the agent
itself were compromised.

30
00:02:09,914 --> 00:02:16,434
In our evidence run, we sent that
payment signed with the agent's own key.

31
00:02:16,514 --> 00:02:19,263
The Mandate hook refused it: SANCTIONED.

32
00:02:19,343 --> 00:02:25,391
The refused attempt is written on Base,
with the reason the contract computed.

33
00:02:25,471 --> 00:02:31,520
Across our red-team suite on the local
fork: 100 attack runs, zero executed.

34
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:34,675
A new payee is different.

35
00:02:34,755 --> 00:02:40,567
Lin asks for 0.15 USDC to an
address the mandate doesn't know.

36
00:02:40,647 --> 00:02:44,496
The contract refuses it
on Base: unknown payee.

37
00:02:44,576 --> 00:02:47,933
This is tier two: it needs Lin.

38
00:02:48,013 --> 00:02:50,388
She opens Praetor inside WeChat.

39
00:02:50,468 --> 00:02:53,825
The phone recomputes the
payment's fingerprint itself

40
00:02:53,905 --> 00:02:57,262
and shows the exact address and amount.

41
00:02:57,342 --> 00:02:59,717
Lin approves with Face ID.

42
00:02:59,797 --> 00:03:03,155
Our attester checks the
signature with Tencent,

43
00:03:03,235 --> 00:03:09,047
and the contract checks the attester's
approval, bound to this one call.

44
00:03:09,127 --> 00:03:10,520
It executes once.

45
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:14,848
The bank knows Lin, and knows her agent.

46
00:03:14,928 --> 00:03:18,929
Her KYC and the agent's mandate
are WeIdentity credentials.

47
00:03:19,009 --> 00:03:22,556
Her personal data stays
encrypted in the bank;

48
00:03:22,636 --> 00:03:27,544
on chain, only identifiers, hashes,
her KYC level, risk profile and country.

49
00:03:27,624 --> 00:03:32,079
Without a valid agent credential,
the contract refuses every call.

50
00:03:32,159 --> 00:03:37,520
Our consortium contracts also pass
a smoke test on FISCO's Guomi build.

51
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:39,777
Now the regulator.

52
00:03:39,857 --> 00:03:44,969
In the consortium console, one
regulator signature freezes Lin's agent.

53
00:03:45,049 --> 00:03:49,121
WeCross carries that
decision from FISCO to Base,

54
00:03:49,201 --> 00:03:53,274
and the hook verifies the
member's signature itself.

55
00:03:53,354 --> 00:03:58,466
The next payment is refused:
FROZEN. Lin's app turns red.

56
00:03:58,546 --> 00:04:06,252
Letting it go takes two of the three
members: here, the regulator and the bank.

57
00:04:06,332 --> 00:04:10,924
And if the operator goes
silent for fifteen minutes,

58
00:04:11,004 --> 00:04:13,520
the agent loses its autonomy.

59
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:16,196
Every action leaves evidence.

60
00:04:16,276 --> 00:04:21,135
Each decision lands in a
hash-chained audit log on FISCO,

61
00:04:21,215 --> 00:04:24,099
anchored on Base by two members,

62
00:04:24,179 --> 00:04:30,520
and exports as an ISO 20022 bank
statement. Lin's bank can verify it.

63
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:33,567
Autonomous. Bounded. Regulated.

64
00:04:33,647 --> 00:04:39,826
Praetor: self-driving money.
The regulator holds the brakes.

65
00:04:39,906 --> 00:04:44,520
Try it at the link below.
